        ":question/id": "3b0fa11c-feb9-540f-a74b-38792fbe2335",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-2385",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{cos\u2061x}{10{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=cos\u2061x$ and $v(x)=10{x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-sin\u2061x)(10{x}^{2})-(cos\u2061x)(20x)}{(10{x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10{x}^{2}sin\u2061x-20xcos\u2061x}{100{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{10x}(-xsin\u2061x-2cos\u2061x)}{\\cancel{10x}\\cdot 10{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-xsin\u2061x-2cos\u2061x}{10{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
