          ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $v(x)=10 x^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (10 x^{2})-(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (20 x)}{(10 x^{2})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{- 10 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 20 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{100 x^{4}}\\\\ &=\\frac{- 10 x \\left(x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}{100 x^{4}}\\\\ &=- \\frac{x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{10 x^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
